                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efcde42d-f917-3081-9ecb-1c746b96202a",
                        "entry_id": "c790fe57-9c50-36e2-84c8-3e86e09a9e5d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "международная солидарность людей различных наций и рас, основа их взаимопонимания, взаимного доверия, взаимопроникновения культур, ценностей, знаний и технологий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02bac906-7934-424d-9817-c09900e17a1f",
                                "sense_id": "efcde42d-f917-3081-9ecb-1c746b96202a",
                                "text": "Он в высшей степени способствует экономическому сближению народов и ему свойственен своеобразный интернационализм."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "859f2035-ab08-3513-9a22-8c964593995b",
                        "entry_id": "c790fe57-9c50-36e2-84c8-3e86e09a9e5d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "лингв., слова, совпадающие в разных языках по своей внешней форме, с полностью или частично совпадающим смыслом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e902ec85-ccf5-4dd9-9d89-6453ee8686de",
                                "sense_id": "859f2035-ab08-3513-9a22-8c964593995b",
                                "text": "Источник интернационализмов — какой-нибудь язык (ср. русский «спутник», немецкий Sputnik, английский sputnic) или греко-латинские корни слов, лежащие в основе интернациональной терминологической лексики."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4a17f6d2-05c9-4b85-985a-9ee50210fa01",
                        "source_entry_id": "c790fe57-9c50-36e2-84c8-3e86e09a9e5d",
                        "target_lang_word": "internationalism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "internationalism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da727d96-12eb-3a31-9e26-89f8493212c4",
                                        "entry_id": "6ee53595-29c7-328a-b9d5-b15a4c0f1567",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Political, economic and cultural cooperation between nations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68e9cbf7-ff34-471b-a588-73d989ad2920",
                                                "sense_id": "da727d96-12eb-3a31-9e26-89f8493212c4",
                                                "text": "Once again the opposite poles of isolationism and Wilsonian internationalism appeared as alternatives that split the liberal and conservative camps"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9bf6647-6653-403e-a34d-5dec3392b7a5",
                                                "sense_id": "da727d96-12eb-3a31-9e26-89f8493212c4",
                                                "text": "One day in the not too distant future, we may look back on Donald Trump’s return to power as the death knell of “liberal internationalism.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9627db1-0514-3cd4-81cd-09985055b375",
                                        "entry_id": "6ee53595-29c7-328a-b9d5-b15a4c0f1567",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A loanword that occurs in several languages with the same or similar meaning and etymology."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8a90f01-8844-3121-abd4-8a63ea23d761",
                                        "entry_id": "6ee53595-29c7-328a-b9d5-b15a4c0f1567",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A major architectural style that was developed in the 1920s and 1930s and was closely related to modernism, characterized by lightweight industrial materials, lack of ornamentation, and flat surfaces."
                                        ],
